documentation='Flux-surface-averaged toroidal nitrogen-ion velocity is the density-weighted mean of the toroidal bulk-flow velocities of nitrogen ions over the separatrix, the plasma boundary between closed and open magnetic field lines. Nitrogen ion charge states are combined as one intensive species quantity; their velocities are averaged, not summed.

The defining charge-state and flux-surface average is

$$
\langle v_{\phi,N}\rangle_{\mathrm{sep}}
=
\frac{\displaystyle\oint_{\mathcal S_{\mathrm{sep}}}
\left(\frac{\sum_{q=1}^{7} n_{N^{q+}}v_{\phi,N^{q+}}}{\sum_{q=1}^{7} n_{N^{q+}}}\right)
\frac{dS}{|\nabla\psi|}}
{\displaystyle\oint_{\mathcal S_{\mathrm{sep}}}\frac{dS}{|\nabla\psi|}}
$$

where $n_{N^{q+}}$ is the number density of nitrogen charge state $q$ in m$^{-3}$, $v_{\phi,N^{q+}}$ is its toroidal velocity component in m s$^{-1}$, $q$ ranges from 1 through 7, $dS$ is a surface-area element, and $\psi$ is a flux-surface label. The toroidal component uses the right-handed cylindrical $(R,\phi,Z)$ frame, where $R$ is major radius, $\phi$ is toroidal angle, and $Z$ is vertical height.

This quantity excludes neutral nitrogen. The related [flux-surface-averaged nitrogen density](name:flux_surface_averaged_nitrogen_density_at_plasma_boundary) is the corresponding charge-state-summed extensive quantity, while [toroidal flux-surface-averaged ion velocity](name:flux_surface_averaged_toroidal_ion_velocity_at_plasma_boundary) combines ion species rather than isolating nitrogen.'; dd_source_docs=[{'id': 'summary/local/separatrix_average/velocity_phi/nitrogen/value', 'unit': 'm.s^-1', 'description': 'Nitrogen (N).', 'documentation': 'Value', 'raw_dd_context': {'path': 'summary/local/separatrix_average/velocity_phi/nitrogen/value', 'dd_version': '4.1.1', 'unit': 'm.s^-1', 'documentation': 'Value', 'data_type': None, 'node_type': None, 'physics_domain': None, 'cocos_transformation_type': None, 'cocos_transformation_expression': None, 'coordinates': [], 'lifecycle_status': None, 'lifecycle_version': None, 'parents': [], 'members': []}, 'published_dd_context': {'path': 'summary/local/separatrix_average/velocity_phi/nitrogen/value', 'dd_version': '4.1.1', 'unit': 'm.s^-1', 'documentation': 'Value', 'data_type': None, 'node_type': None, 'physics_domain': None, 'cocos_transformation_type': None, 'cocos_transformation_expression': None, 'coordinates': [], 'lifecycle_status': None, 'lifecycle_version': None, 'parents': [], 'members': []}, 'dd_resolution_ids': [], 'dd_resolution_converged_ids': [], 'dd_resolution_manifest_digest': 'sha256:02dd37c745ddff3802f6d1fc577e7dbfe0c5b9832f69a149db5f78188ba4361d'}]; description='Flux-surface-averaged toroidal velocity of nitrogen ions at the plasma boundary (separatrix), with charge states combined by a density-weighted mean.'

